const entries = [
 {key:"war-dorgath",name:"Dorgath Zharmog, Watch-Captain",art:"assets/tokens/tokens-01/orcs-and-half-orcs/orc-battle-driver.png",zone:"docks",doing:"Standing at the head of the dock in full blackened mail, a glaive grounded beside him, counting the party before they land.",bio:"<p>Dorgath commands the Vrokmar watch and wears the best mail Drogar ever made. He marched under the war-banner in his younger years and came home when the Fire Council asked for a steady hand, and he has been steady ever since. He is courteous to strangers in the exact way a closed gate is courteous.</p>",gm:"<p>He fought beside Bazrak's sons and knows Bazgar by face and by name: he greets him as \"Bazrak's second\" and asks after the famous brother with a look that says he knows the two do not agree. The watch's rule is his: strangers get guest-right at the fire until dawn, and after dark nobody goes past the docks without a hearth-member's word. He knows about the drylander boat Urgha found and is deciding whether these strangers came in it.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmWarriorVeteran",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-battle-driver-2dfa7b.webp"},
 {key:"war-grukh",name:"Grukh Drokmar, Watch-Warrior",art:"assets/tokens/tokens-01/orcs-and-half-orcs/orc-warrior-on-snow.png",zone:"edge-watch",doing:"Thigh-deep at the reed-line post with an axe across his shoulders, as still as a heron, water running off his mail.",bio:"<p>Grukh has stood the edge watch longer than its captain has been alive and has no intention of stopping. He is grey, scarred and wet most of the day, and says perhaps ten words in it. The young warriors learn stillness from him or they learn it from the fen.</p>",gm:"<p>For three nights the fen east of his post has gone silent at dusk: no frogs, no night-birds, and the water there runs cold where the warm springs should keep it mild. He has moved the post ten paces nearer the hearth without telling Dorgath, which he has never done in his life. He will speak to a warrior who stands still beside him for a while, and not otherwise.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmWarriorInfantr",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-warrior-on-snow-1b7a26.webp"},
 {key:"war-vashka",name:"Vashka Gronmog, Watch-Warrior",art:"assets/tokens/tokens-01/orcs-and-half-orcs/orc-paladin.png",zone:"boardwalk",doing:"Walking the boardwalk in blackened mail, testing each plank with her heel and keeping the strangers in the corner of her eye.",bio:"<p>Vashka is Drogar's sister and wears the first hauberk he ever made that he was satisfied with. She walks the boardwalks from the shrine to the racks and back, and she has never once lost count of who is on them. She is polite, direct and entirely unimpressed by titles.</p>",gm:"<p>She will recite the watch's rule on strangers after dark without being asked, and she wants a straight answer about what the party is doing in the fen; she will know if she does not get one. Tell: she touches the twin-flame etching on her gorget when she is lying, which she does badly and rarely.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmWarriorInfantr",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-paladin-24e728.webp"},
 {key:"war-rukka",name:"Rukka Krulmar, Watch-Warrior",art:"modules/dnd-players-handbook/assets/tokens/orc-03.webp",zone:"edge-watch",doing:"At the watch post nearest the path, gripping her axe too tightly and trying to look older than she is.",bio:"<p>Rukka took the watch-oath this season and still stands as if the axe might get away from her. She is Brug's eldest and Zhulka's niece, trained by Grukh, and determined that nothing will get past her post in her first year. She blushes dark when spoken to and answers anyway.</p>",gm:"<p>The missing boy in Ruzga's canoe is her cousin, and she is one quiet night away from leaving her post to look for him; a word from a stranger who seems capable might tip her into asking them to go instead. She will blurt out anything the watch has been told to keep quiet, including the drylander boat.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmWarriorInfantr",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-03-1b180d.webp"},
 {key:"war-thrak",name:"Thrak Vrokmar, Hearth-Guard",art:"assets/tokens/tokens-01/orcs-and-half-orcs/orc-barbarian-with-giant-axe.png",zone:"edge-watch",doing:"Leaning on the haft of an enormous blackened axe where the path meets the boardwalk, watching the strangers without blinking.",bio:"<p>Thrak is the biggest orc in the hearth and the quietest, a cousin of Vraka's who came home from the war-bands and asked for nothing but a post he could hold. He holds the path. Children climb him; strangers do not, and he does not need to say so.</p>",gm:"<p>He will not move for anyone without Dorgath's or Vraka's word, and he means it. He is the only one who has gone up the east channel since the canoe vanished; he found the traps lifted and the catch still in them, rotting, and no sign of either pole. He told Vraka and no one else.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmBerserker00000",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-barbarian-with-giant-axe-29b0b9.webp"}
