const entries = [
 {key:"civ-brug",name:"Brug Krulmar, Hearth-Cook",art:"modules/dnd-players-handbook/assets/tokens/orc-01.webp",zone:"cook-fire",doing:"Stirring a black cauldron of eel and reed-root stew with a marsh hawk perched on his forearm, scolding a child away from the pot.",bio:"<p>Brug feeds the Vrokmar hearth and considers it the most important post in it, which no one who has eaten his eel stew argues with. His hawk, Pike, rides his arm all day and gets the first scrap of anything that comes off the fire. He is loud, generous and watches strangers the way he watches a pot about to boil over.</p>",gm:"<p>He knows Vraka is failing and the hearth is quietly afraid of what happens when she goes; he wants the strangers fed, guest-right given and the party on their way before dark so nothing upsets her. He will hand a bowl to anyone who sits down, which under hearth custom is guest-right until the next dawn.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmCommoner000000",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-01-43a840.webp"},
 {key:"civ-drogar",name:"Drogar Gronmog, Black-Iron Smith",art:"assets/tokens/tokens-01/orcs-and-half-orcs/orc-chieftain.png",zone:"forge",doing:"Arms up, drawing a glowing spearhead out of the kiln and plunging it into a trough of alligator fat; the steam stinks and rolls across the boardwalk.",bio:"<p>Drogar runs the Cold-Blooded Kiln at the edge of the hearth and turns out the blackened iron the Dakmar'nak are known for. It is quenched in alligator fat over peat charcoal so it will not rust in the fen, and he is prouder of a good fish-hook than a good sword. He is broad, burned along both forearms, and will tell you, unasked, which of your weapons will rust first.</p>",gm:"<p>A drylander at the reed-bank trade meet asked him, twice, how the blackening is done and offered good salt for it; he refused and remembers the man's face. He sizes up every blade the party carries and names the one that is going to fail them, which is accurate. He wants peat charcoal cut from the east bank and nobody will go there now.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmTough000000000",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-chieftain-3e08ca.webp"},
 {key:"civ-skarn",name:"Skarn Drokmar, Hide-Tanner",art:"assets/tokens/tokens-01/orcs-and-half-orcs/orc-swashbuckler.png",zone:"water-edge",doing:"Shouldering a rolled cold-water alligator hide up from the bank, where two more are pegged out and half scraped.",bio:"<p>Skarn works the hides of the cold-water alligators, the warm-blooded ones the hearth reveres and hunts only with an offering first. He scrapes them on the bank, cures them in peat smoke and lacquers the finished leather with iron-birch sap. He smells of all three and does not apologise for it.</p>",gm:"<p>He knows the alligators have moved away from the east channel, all of them, which in his lifetime they have never done; whatever is in that water, the gators will not share it. He takes that as a worse sign than anything the shamans have said, and will say so to anyone who asks about the hides.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmCommoner000000",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-swashbuckler-7e5867.webp"},
 {key:"civ-hazg",name:"Hazg Vrokmar, Eel-Smoker",art:"modules/dnd-players-handbook/assets/tokens/orc-04.webp",zone:"smokehouse-racks",doing:"Turning rows of split eel on the smoking racks and waving a greeting with a hand that is still steaming.",bio:"<p>Hazg smokes the eel that keeps the hearth through the frozen months and trades the surplus down the hidden channels. He is the cheerful one, the first to wave and the last to stop talking, and he wears a drylander's wide straw hat he took in trade and loves out of all proportion. His smoked eel is the hearth's handshake to outsiders.</p>",gm:"<p>He trades with Brenfen's eel-smokers at a reed bank a half-day downstream, smoked eel and lacquer for salt and grain. The Brenfen folk were frightened at the last meet, bought iron hooks they did not need and spoke of trouble in their own village after dark; he thinks it is a dryland story and would like someone to tell him it is.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmCommoner000000",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-04-580e79.webp"},
 {key:"civ-zhulka",name:"Zhulka Krulmar, Eel-Fisher",art:"assets/tokens/tokens-01/orcs-and-half-orcs/orc-warrior.png",zone:"docks",doing:"Crouched at the dock edge baiting willow eel-traps with gutted frog, her pole-boat tied up beside her and not yet loaded.",bio:"<p>Zhulka runs the eel lines in the slow channels around the hearth and knows every sinkhole and every gator's hummock between here and the open fen. She is quiet, quick and does not waste words on people who are not going to help her. Her daughter Tazka is the one with the fish-hawk.</p>",gm:"<p>Her sister Ruzga and Ruzga's boy took a canoe east to lift traps and did not come back. The watch-captain has forbidden her to go after them alone and she means to go anyway, tonight; she is quietly weighing whether strangers with weapons are worth the risk of asking.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmCommoner000000",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-warrior-8ce30a.webp"},
 {key:"civ-urgha",name:"Urgha Zharmog, Canoe-Keeper",art:"assets/tokens/tokens-01/pirates-and-sailors/orc-pirate.png",zone:"canoes",doing:"Masked against the fumes, brushing iron-birch lacquer onto an upturned hull among the drawn-up canoes.",bio:"<p>Urgha keeps the hearth's canoes: she lacquers the hulls with iron-birch sap, counts them in at dusk and knows each one by the sound it makes on the water. Nothing leaves the bank without her nod. She works with a cloth over her face and a black three-cornered hat from somewhere far downstream, and the hearth has given up asking about either.</p>",gm:"<p>She is a canoe short (Ruzga's) and has not stopped counting. Yesterday she also found a flat-bottomed drylander boat, not hearth work, dragged up on a hummock downstream with no tracks leading away from it; she has told the captain, who has told no one else yet.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmCommoner000000",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-pirate-bf968d.webp"},
 {key:"civ-mogruk",name:"Old Mogruk Vrokmar, Hearth-Elder",art:"assets/tokens/tokens-01/orcs-and-half-orcs/orc-blue.png",zone:"pavilion",doing:"Sitting on the pavilion steps with a slate on his knees, waiting for pupils who have all run off to look at the strangers.",bio:"<p>Mogruk sat a seat on the Fire Council and gave it up when his knees did, and now drills the hearth's children in spirit-law, the shape of the world and the customs of the people who call them savages. He is bone-thin, bone-strung and sharp enough to argue a visitor to a standstill on whose law is older. He is also the one who decides, with Vraka, whether guest-right stands.</p>",gm:"<p>His younger brother drowned in the fen years back and the Ancestor Fen gave him back three nights after his burial, walking and wrong; Vraka put him down with vines and salt and Mogruk helped her. He has never spoken of it and will, if the party mentions walking dead, go very still and then ask exactly what they saw.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmCommoner000000",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-blue-fd8bfa.webp"},
 {key:"civ-tazka",name:"Tazka Krulmar",art:"modules/dnd-players-handbook/assets/tokens/orc-02.webp",zone:"hut-door",doing:"In a hut doorway feeding scraps to a fish-hawk on her fist, watching the newcomers over its wing.",bio:"<p>Tazka is Zhulka's girl, old enough to run her own trap line and young enough to be told she cannot yet. She has trained a fish-hawk to drive eels into the shallows, which no one else in the hearth has managed, and she is unbearable about it. She wants to be a shaman and Ozha teases her for it.</p>",gm:"<p>Her hawk will not fly east any more; it turns back over the reed line every time, and she thinks the bird knows something the grown-ups will not say. She also knows the way to the Brenfen trade bank and would show it in exchange for being taken seriously.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmCommoner000000",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-02-201095.webp"},
 {key:"civ-brakk",name:"Little Brakk Gronmog",art:"assets/tokens/tokens-01/orcs-and-half-orcs/orc-mage.png",zone:"cook-fire",doing:"Crouched behind the cook with a stolen strip of smoked eel in each fist, about to be caught.",bio:"<p>Brakk is Drogar's youngest and the hearth's most dedicated thief of eel. He can already recite the names of twelve land-spirits and the three rules of guest-right, and will do so for anyone who stands still. He has decided strangers are the most interesting thing to happen all season.</p>",gm:"<p>He found a silver coin in the black mud by the east channel, stamped with a face nobody in the hearth knows, and keeps it in his cheek. He will show it to a stranger who gives him something to eat. He also knows where Tazka hides when she sneaks off to the water at night.</p>",uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmCommoner000000",subject:"assets/tokens/custom/ring-subjects/orc-mage-91410e.webp"}
